# business-os — repo-root .env
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in. Every component loads this file
# itself; nothing is inherited from your shell profile, because nothing that
# matters here runs from your shell.
#
# TWO PARSERS READ THIS FILE, and they do not agree:
#
#   - The Python components parse it line by line (see load_env() in
#     scripts/telegram.py). Bare KEY=value, quotes optional.
#   - The shell components SOURCE it (lib/eng-env.sh). That makes every line a
#     shell statement, so an unquoted value containing a space, a parenthesis or
#     a `#` is a syntax error — and sourcing ABORTS at the first bad line, so
#     every variable BELOW it silently does not exist.
#
# That failure has happened here before, which is why eng-env.sh now warns when
# the source fails. QUOTE ANY VALUE THAT IS NOT a bare word.
#
#   RIGHT:  REDDIT_USER_AGENT="windows:business-os-listener:v1.0 (by /u/you)"
#   WRONG:  REDDIT_USER_AGENT=windows:business-os-listener:v1.0 (by /u/you)


# ── The pause switch ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# sabbath | retreat | quiet  -> every component in every department exits
# immediately and silently. Empty means normal operation.
#
# The scheduler keeps firing either way; the check happens INSIDE each
# component. That is deliberate: a paused system that is still being scheduled
# resumes by itself when you clear this, with nothing to re-install.
#
# This is the GLOBAL switch. To pause one business only, set `mode:` in
# instances/<business>/engineering/config/config.yaml instead — that wins over
# this value, so a single business can be stopped without stopping the rest.
MODE=


# ── Engineering department ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# departments/engineering + instances/*/engineering.

# Where gate decisions reach the approver. Without it the department still runs
# and still queues gate items in the instance inbox and the control center —
# but nothing tells you a decision is waiting, which for a system built on a
# human-in-the-loop approval step means the board stops silently.
# lib/eng-notify.sh posts here; it is the only notification channel implemented.
SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Optional. Overrides the claude binary lib/run-claude.sh execs. Only needed for
# an install in a non-standard location — the resolver already checks
# ~/.local/bin/claude and then PATH.
# ENG_CLAUDE_BIN=

# Optional. Seconds before a single pass is killed and its lock released.
# lib/eng-trigger.sh sets 1800 by default.
# ENG_PASS_TIMEOUT=1800


# ── Reddit marketing pipeline ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# scripts/*.py. Leave blank if you are only running the engineering department.

# Twenty CRM — the system of record for Marketing Content records.
TWENTY_API_KEY=
TWENTY_BASE_URL=

# Telegram — the human approval channel. `python scripts/telegram.py discover`
# prints the chat id once the bot has seen a message in the group.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
AGENT_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# Reddit, READ-ONLY (scripts/reddit_listen.py). A "script" app from
# https://www.reddit.com/prefs/apps. Note the quotes on the user agent.
REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=
REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=
REDDIT_USER_AGENT="windows:business-os-listener:v1.0 (by /u/your-account)"

# Reddit, WRITE (scripts/reddit_post.py — the only component that posts).
# Keep these SEPARATE from the read-only credentials above. Either a refresh
# token, or username + password.
# REDDIT_REFRESH_TOKEN=
# REDDIT_USERNAME=
# REDDIT_PASSWORD=


# ── Control Center ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# control-center/server.py — http://localhost:6789, and (once
# control-center/cloudflare-tunnel.sh is set up) the same dashboard over the
# internet.
#
# THIS LINE IS A SEED, NOT THE USER LIST. It is read exactly once, the first
# time the server starts with no control-center/users.json, and ignored on
# every start after that. Editing it later changes nothing — the Partners tab
# (admin only) owns users from then on, because a role, a phone number and an
# instance assignment have nowhere to live in a comma-separated line, and
# because a page that adds a user must not be rewriting a file lib/eng-env.sh
# sources.
#
# Comma-separated `email:pin`; email is matched case-insensitively. On seeding,
# CONTROL_CENTER_ADMIN (below) becomes the admin and everyone else becomes a
# partner assigned to every instance that exists at that moment — so nobody
# loses the access they had, and the admin narrows it from the Partners tab.
CONTROL_CENTER_USERS=businesspilot.care@gmail.com:6977,h@aiorders.io:1212

# Optional. Which seeded email becomes the admin. Defaults to h@aiorders.io,
# falling back to the first entry above if that email is not in the list. Only
# consulted during seeding; after that, roles are changed on the Partners tab.
# CONTROL_CENTER_ADMIN=h@aiorders.io

# Only needed for control-center/cloudflare-tunnel.sh. The hostname the
# Control Center should answer on over the internet; its domain must already
# be a zone in the Cloudflare account you run `cloudflared tunnel login` as.
CONTROL_CENTER_TUNNEL_HOSTNAME=control.aiorders.io

# ── Claude Code headless auth ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# departments/engineering/lib/run-claude.sh execs the `claude` CLI directly,
# so without a token here every automated build-loop pass authenticates as
# whatever account is logged into `claude` interactively on this machine — and
# an interactive /login elsewhere on the host silently swaps the account the
# passes run as. A token pins them to one specific account: it outranks the
# /login session in the CLI's own credential precedence. Generate one
# interactively on any machine with a browser (needs a Pro/Max/Team/Enterprise
# plan on the account the passes should run as):
#   claude setup-token
# Valid for a year. Leave blank to fall back to the interactive CLI login.
#
# MORE THAN ONE ACCOUNT — number them, up to _9. The build loop uses one at a
# time, in this order; when the one in force hits a usage/rate/spend limit it
# marks that account blocked and rotates to the next unblocked one on the very
# next fire, with no back-off. The exponential back-off in
# departments/engineering/lib/eng-trigger.sh is armed only once EVERY account
# has hit a limit — and arming it unblocks them all, so the retry after that
# window starts again at the first account.
#
# Which account is in force lives in
# instances/{business}/engineering/traces/.oauth-account (first field is the
# index into this list, the rest are the blocked ones). Delete it to reset.
#
# Numbered rather than one comma-separated value because this file is both
# sourced by lib/eng-env.sh and parsed line-by-line by the Python components.
# Gaps are skipped: deleting _2 and keeping _3 still gives you two accounts.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
#CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN_2=
#CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN_3=
#
# These are the HOST's tokens, and they drive the engineering build loop. A
# PARTNER's own token is a different thing and does not belong here: it is
# per-person, they enter it themselves on the Control Center's Config tab, and
# it is stored in control-center/partner-config.json (gitignored, 0600)
# alongside their SMS gateway and customer-database credentials. Nothing in
# this file is consulted for partner work.
